  {
   "instrument_id": "EO:7831",
   "outcome": "blocked",
   "reason": "[\"The only registered text of EO 8704 (the superseding order, 6 FR 1302) is an OCR layer that prints the footnote marks fused into the amended-order numbers (78311, 84403, 86744); the actual checker rejects that quotation (order_exists:not_in_universe). A clean held text of EO 8704 (jobs/app-executive-orders output) is not registered as citable evidence in this packet, so the supersession cannot be quoted from a registered source; a source supplement adding the 8704 sentence is needed.\"]"
  },
  {
   "instrument_id": "EO:7845",
   "outcome": "blocked",
   "reason": "Independent review did not uphold this version: [{\"field\": \"operative_clauses[sec6-r1].later_events[0].effective_date\", \"claim_says\": \"1938-05-09 (EO 7879 restatement of section 6)\", \"source_says\": \"EO 7879: 'This order shall be effective as of January 1, 1938'. The claim's own judgment_reason says 'effective as of January 1, 1938'. Because 7845 itself took effect as of January 1, 1938, the restated section 6 displaced the original wording from the order's own effective date.\"}, {\"field\": \"operative_clauses[sec15-r1].later_events[0].effective_date\", \"claim_says\": \"1939-08-24 (EO 8226 restatement of section 15)\", \"source_says\": \"EO 8226: 'This order shall be effective as of June 30, 1939'. The claim's judgment_reason says 'effective as of June 30, 1939', so the effective_date field contradicts the claim's own text.\"}, {\"field\": \"research_rationale / earlier_end_check\", \"claim_says\": \"whole supersession by EO 8384, with no mention of the packet conflict\", \"source_says\": \"the packet dossier records FULL_AND_PARTIAL_EVIDENCE_CONFLICT for EO 8384, because the OFR note on 7845 reads 'EO 8384, March 29, 1940 (in part)'. The claim neither resolves nor discloses this conflict; the held 8384 text ('This order shall supersede Executive Orders No. 7845') supports a whole supersession, but the brief requires the conflict to be resolved on the record.\"}, {\"field\": \"savings_residuals.reason\", \"claim_says\": \"8384's supersession provision 'provides that leave credited ... may not exceed the amount authorized ... so leave credits earned under 7845 carried into the new regime'\", \"source_says\": \"the 8384 proviso caps leave produced by adjusting leave under the amended sections 6 and 9. It does not state a carry-forward. The carry-forward is the producer's inference and is presented as what the provision provides.\"}]"
  },
